# Patch-ID: P-TAB-001 / P-APP-001 / P-NAV-001 (wave 10, core C ABI)
# Area: tab.
# Rationale: Swift needs a C-only exported interface for browser-less tabs,
#   navigation, profile identity, native attachment ownership and orderly quit.
# Last-Rebased: 2026-11-02 (Chromium 156.0.8078.74).
# Frozen-file exceptions: profile registry gains monotonic IDs/keepalives;
#   TabSession captures profile ID; typed tab/service emitters stamp identity;
#   close_controller captures profile before removal and signals real destruction.
#   TabRegistry adds ID enumeration for shutdown; adoption uses common observer
#   initialization; observer refreshes URL/history after navigation and captures
#   terminal identity. These dormant seams cannot be connected additively alone.
#   attachment_lease gains occlusion and uses UpdateWebContentsVisibility: the
#   public API explicitly requires it for first VISIBLE at this pin. Earlier
#   entry version now CHECKs main and reports the new implementation version.
#   No earlier bridge BUILD.gn edit; minimal browser :core source block and
#   framework export/order lists only. All other upstream C++ untouched.
# Policy: C ABI 1 is an in-process adapter, synchronous returns replace create/
#   attach replies; all callbacks are queued and copied on Chromium UI. Startup
#   wrapper uses upstream no-startup-window policy, never creates Browser UI.
#   Only startup profile admitted. HTTP(S)/about:blank navigation; no JS/file/
#   chrome navigation capability. Physical upstream app/helper layout required.
# Gate: build-p21 green attempt 2, post-format p22 green; G1-G5 PASS;
#   assembled native ABI lifecycle PASS runtime-tab017c.log; C header PASS.
#   nm -gU: 27 definitions in libchrome_dll (component framework reexport stub);
#   dlsym through framework PASS all 27, nm-tab017.log. Release lists updated;
#   non-component build/standalone Swift packaging not claimed.
# Integrity: sequential full-series temporary-index reverse/forward replay.
